-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Maintainer check before each release: this list was written by reading go.mod, the
package.json files of app/ and phone/, and the asset folders. Re-check it when a
dependency or an asset is added.

1. Linked into the `wy` binary (Go modules, from go.mod)

   github.com/pelletier/go-toml/v2        MIT
   golang.org/x/sys                       BSD-3-Clause
   golang.org/x/term                      BSD-3-Clause
   modernc.org/sqlite                     BSD-3-Clause (includes SQLite, public domain)
   modernc.org/libc                       BSD-3-Clause (includes parts of musl libc, MIT)
   modernc.org/mathutil                   BSD-3-Clause
   modernc.org/memory                     BSD-3-Clause
   rsc.io/qr                              BSD-3-Clause
   github.com/coder/websocket             ISC
   github.com/dustin/go-humanize          MIT
   github.com/google/uuid                 BSD-3-Clause
   github.com/mattn/go-isatty             MIT
   github.com/ncruces/go-strftime         MIT
   github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft       BSD-3-Clause

2. Bundled into the desktop app packages (app/)

   Electron and Chromium, under their own licenses (MIT, BSD-3-Clause and others).
   electron-builder writes LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html into every
   package. The packages also contain a copy of `wy` (section 1).

3. Bundled into the Android app (phone/)

   React Native, Expo SDK modules, expo-router, react-native-android-widget,
   react-native-screens, react-native-safe-area-context and
   @react-native-async-storage/async-storage, each under its own license (MIT for all of
   them at the pinned versions in phone/package.json), and the AndroidX and Kotlin
   libraries they pull in (Apache-2.0). Watchyard's own Android modules (phone/modules) add:
   OkHttp and Tink (Apache-2.0) in wy-link; ShortcutBadger (Apache-2.0, Leo Lin) for the
   launcher badge in wy-notify; and zxing-android-embedded (Apache-2.0, JourneyApps) with
   ZXing core (Apache-2.0, ZXing authors) for the QR scanner in wy-scan. The APK contains no
   proprietary Google code: no Firebase, Google Play services or ML Kit
   (phone/scripts/check-no-google.mjs, docs/spec/phone.md P13).

   Build tools and data used while building the Android app (not shipped as code in the
   APK, listed for completeness):
   node-forge        (BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0); Watchyard uses it under BSD-3-Clause
   lightningcss      MPL-2.0, used unmodified by the Metro bundler
   caniuse-lite      CC-BY-4.0, browser support data, (c) Alexis Deveria and contributors

4. Fonts and icons

   IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, Copyright IBM Corp., licensed under the SIL Open Font
   License 1.1. The web board serves them itself (self-hosted with its static files, together
   with the OFL text); the desktop app names the same fonts and falls back to system fonts.

   Noto Sans Math, Noto Sans Symbols and Noto Sans Symbols 2, Copyright 2022 Google LLC and
   The Noto Project Authors, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Three subsets of
   about 3 KB in all (the arrows, shapes and marks the board draws, which Plex lacks) are
   served by the web board next to the Plex files under webui/static/fonts, from the
   @fontsource packages of the same names, with the OFL text.

   Every icon and image in this repository (app/assets, app/build, phone/assets,
   webui/static/icons, scripts/icons) is original Watchyard artwork, drawn from the SVG
   sources in app/build/icons-src, phone/assets/src and scripts/icons. No Anthropic logo or
   mark is used.
